  "body": "According to @natechapin, this is true in Blink, and probably inherited from WebKit.\r\n\r\nWhereas in the spec, this appears to only be done for [Location-object setter navigate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#location-object-setter-navigate). (Not even Location-object navigate in general, so the spec says it doesn't apply to `location.assign()`!)\r\n\r\nI'll try to write up a series of tests and a spec patch for this. Hopefully there's a clear 2/3 behavior.\r\n\r\n(FYI, this was discovered as part of the [app history](https://github.com/WICG/app-history) work, in particular speccing `appHistory.navigate()`. And I did promise that we'd try to fix foundational interop issues we found while working on app history!!)\r\n\r\nThis appears to be the same issue as https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3247 so Firefox has had compat problems in the past and already diverged from the spec a bit by adding a form submission special case, it seems. /cc @smaug---- for a Gecko FYI.\r\n\r\n/cc @rakina since this is somewhat similar in spirit to #6491.",
